          "en": "to this summary item widget here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 271.47,
          "end": 274.74,
          "en": "and I'm taken right to the code line in my case here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 274.74,
          "end": 278.283,
          "en": "line 25, that seems to be causing this error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 279.15,
          "end": 282.45,
          "en": "Now combined with the error message, the problem here seems",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 282.45,
          "end": 287.4,
          "en": "to be that we are trying to cast something to int so",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 287.4,
          "end": 289.08,
          "en": "that we're trying to tell Dart",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 289.08,
          "end": 291.75,
          "en": "that some value is of type int.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 291.75,
          "end": 294.93,
          "en": "That's what we're doing here with this piece of code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 294.93,
          "end": 299.52,
          "en": "when the value actually is of type string and dart",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 299.52,
          "end": 303.72,
          "en": "therefore complains here at runtime when executing the app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 303.72,
          "end": 305.49,
          "en": "that it can't treat a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 305.49,
          "end": 308.013,
          "en": "as an integer even if we wanted to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 308.97,
          "end": 311.61,
          "en": "So the problem here seems to be that the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 311.61,
          "end": 315.36,
          "en": "that we think is an end is actually a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 315.36,
          "end": 317.01,
          "en": "And this is a great starting point",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 317.01,
          "end": 318.81,
          "en": "to dive deeper into this error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 318.81,
          "end": 322.35,
          "en": "and into this bug that seems to exist in this app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 322.35,
          "end": 325.293,
          "en": "What is inside of item data question?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 327.15,
          "end": 329.76,
          "en": "Well, we can go to the results screen, which is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 329.76,
          "end": 333.15,
          "en": "where this map object here is constructed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 333.15,
          "end": 335.28,
          "en": "And there we can take a look at the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 335.28,
          "end": 337.83,
          "en": "that has this question key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 337.83,
          "end": 340.713,
          "en": "because it is this question key we're accessing here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 341.737,
          "end": 345.54,
          "en": "Now if we take a look at that key, we can indeed confirm",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 345.54,
          "end": 347.97,
          "en": "that there seems to be a string stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 347.97,
          "end": 350.15999999999997,
          "en": "as a value for that key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 350.15999999999997,
          "end": 352.59000000000003,
          "en": "So indeed here the problem simply is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 352.59000000000003,
          "end": 356.94,
          "en": "that we are accidentally accessing the wrong key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 356.94,
          "end": 359.73,
          "en": "This here should be question index",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 359.73,
          "end": 361.95,
          "en": "because it's that question index key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 361.95,
          "end": 364.74,
          "en": "that contains an integer as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 364.74,
          "end": 368.46,
          "en": "Now because this map has a value type of object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 368.46,
          "end": 372.36,
          "en": "to accept different value types, DART was not able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 372.36,
          "end": 375.09,
          "en": "to catch this error during development.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 375.09,
          "end": 378.33,
          "en": "It doesn't show any error here in the IDE when using the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 378.33,
          "end": 382.02,
          "en": "wrong key because it simply doesn't store any specific type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 382.02,
          "end": 384.09,
          "en": "information about the values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 384.09,
          "end": 386.19,
          "en": "Instead, it only knows that any kind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 386.19,
          "end": 389.28,
          "en": "of value is accepted here for those keys.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 389.28,
          "end": 391.62,
          "en": "But of course at runtime, when this code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 391.62,
          "end": 394.44,
          "en": "really executes, this crashes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 394.44,
          "end": 397.8,
          "en": "because question as it turns out, stores a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 397.8,
          "end": 399.51,
          "en": "and not an integer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 399.51,
          "end": 403.68,
          "en": "So here the fix is to use question index instead,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 403.68,
          "end": 407.52,
          "en": "which is the correct key that does store an integer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 407.52,
